WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.360
If you plan on going into Avengers: Endgame
completely spoiler-free, well best of luck

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:05.960
to you.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.100
But if you really just can't wait for your
next Endgame fix, these leaks and spoilers

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.780
should tide you over until April.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.980
Sometimes it isn't what a Marvel actor says
that gives the game away, but where they say

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:18.480
it.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.380
In August 2018, fans noticed that a certain
behind-the-scenes interview with Robert Downey

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.120
Jr. seemed to take place on the set of Shuri's
lab in Wakanda.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:32.460
Taking this at face value, it would seem to
imply that Tony Stark is going to Wakanda

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.820
— and could meet the young Wakandan genius
herself.

00:00:35.540 --> 00:00:39.720
The second Endgame trailer revealed what we
all knew was going to happen - Tony Stark

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:40.980
makes it back to Earth.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.980
Once home, it looks like he and Shuri could
combine their considerable brainpower and

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:50.000
scientific know-how to give the Avengers a
chance to put things right.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:55.079
Unfortunately, Marvel threw a curveball during
the Endgame trailer by having Shuri's face

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.180
flash up on one of Bruce Banner's monitors,
implying that she was lost during the Decimation.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:05.280
This is despite Angela Bassett, who plays
Queen Ramonda, having already confirmed to

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:07.740
ScreenRant that she and Shuri both survived.

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:13.720
Obviously Thanos will return in Endgame but
will he really be the lead villain?

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:18.580
Long before Avengers 4 had even been given
a title, tie-in merch for the movie seemed

00:01:18.580 --> 00:01:21.300
to drop a potentially huge spoiler for the
story.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:26.320
The packaging, which showed Thor and Rocket
Raccoon kitted out with brand new matching

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:31.390
costumes, included a short synopsis that seemingly
confirmed a new villain would come to the

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:32.440
fore in Endgame.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.280
It read:

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:38.140
"The Asgardian Thor wields the mighty Stormbreaker
in his battle against new foes.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.820
Rocket teams up with a new crew to guard the
galaxy from an even greater threat."

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:46.780
“Aw, what the hell.

00:01:46.780 --> 00:01:47.780
I don’t got that long a lifespan anyway.”

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:50.720
But who or what could this "greater threat"
be?

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:55.750
If Endgame follows the plot of the Infinity
Gauntlet comic, Nebula could end up as the

00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:00.320
main antagonist but there are a whole host
of other villains who could end up facing

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.440
down the Avengers.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.120
Of course, it’s entirely possible that Thanos
is the primary villain for Endgame after all,

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.440
and that this “greater threat” is a terrifying
new plan that he’s putting into action.

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:12.700
Who knows?

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:19.780
In October 2018, TheWrap exclusively revealed
that 13 Reasons Why star Katherine Langford

00:02:19.780 --> 00:02:24.450
had joined the cast of the upcoming Avengers
sequel in a mystery role, and various other

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.740
media outlets quickly backed the story up.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.020
The Hollywood Reporter later confirmed:

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.360
"Langford has filmed scenes for the currently
untitled Avengers 4.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.580
Character details were not available, and
Marvel Studios had no comment."

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.240
MovieWeb sources claimed that Langford had
already finished all of her filming for the

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.910
movie, suggesting that she was brought on
board in a relatively minor role and did what

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.020
she needed to do during the September 2018
reshoots.

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:55.430
So Langford's part probably won't be a big
one, but if it was little more than glorified

00:02:55.430 --> 00:03:00.040
extra work then Marvel wouldn't have gone
to the trouble of hiring an in-demand star.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:05.530
She got a much-deserved nod at the Golden
Globes 2018 for her work as Hannah Baker in

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:10.860
teen drama 13 Reasons Why, the first season
of which was a massive hit for Netflix.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:16.140
Marvel and Disney clearly know a rising star
when they see one, but just how important

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:18.660
Langford is to Endgame has yet to be seen.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:24.140
Don Cheadle's Colonel James Rhodes was badly
injured during the events of Captain America:

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:28.880
Civil War, but Tony Stark's loyal Air Force
buddy came back from the brink of paralysis

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:31.560
to join the fight against Thanos in Infinity
War.

00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.240
Rhodey was one of the few heroes who survived
the Mad Titan's mass genocide in that movie,

00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:41.680
meaning he'll be among those who rally against
the villain in Endgame and he'll apparently

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:44.280
be doing so in some badass new armor.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.300
Boom, you looking for this?”

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:56.160
Toy-related leaks have been coming thick and
fast as Endgame’s release draws ever closer,

00:03:56.620 --> 00:04:00.760
and while the Russo brothers have insisted
that the vast majority of these toys are not

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:05.569
reflective of the movie's actual plot, the
sibling directors have been known to tell

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:08.720
little white lies in order to throw fans off
the scent.

00:04:09.209 --> 00:04:13.700
Images of what appear to be official Endgame
LEGO sets are now online, and there's every

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:15.520
reason to believe they're the real deal.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:20.739
One set that is already being sold in the
UK is titled “War Machine Buster”.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:25.240
As the name suggests, it's a Hulkbuster style
version of Rhodey's War Machine armor.

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:30.060
This isn't official confirmation that we'll
see Rhodey in new, pimped-out armor during

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:35.760
Endgame, but the fact that the set also includes
War Machine and Ant-Man minifigures suggests

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:41.000
that we might indeed, since the two characters
are shown suiting up side-by-side in Endgame’s

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:42.100
Super Bowl TV spot.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:49.300
Despite starring in 2011's Thor and its 2013
follow-up Thor: The Dark World, Natalie Portman's

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:54.280
Jane Foster was nowhere to be seen in the
trilogy’s wildly successful threequel, Thor:

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:54.880
Ragnarok.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:56.550
“Sorry to hear that Jane dumped you.”

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.740
“She didn’t dump me, you know.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:00.740
I dumped her.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:01.620
it was a mutual dumping.”

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:05.760
Portman is said to have fallen out of love
with Marvel Studios during the course of the

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:10.840
much-maligned The Dark World, displeased that
future Wonder Woman director Patty Jenkins

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:12.180
was let go from the project.

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:17.180
But Marvel has changed since then, and so
has Portman's stance on the franchise.

00:05:17.640 --> 00:05:22.840
When she spoke to ScreenRant in early 2018,
the Oscar winner revealed that she was actually

00:05:22.850 --> 00:05:27.730
open to reprising the role in future movies,
though she hadn't heard anything from Marvel

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:28.460
at that time.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:33.500
It seems the Russo brothers got this message
loud and clear, because when they were asked

00:05:33.510 --> 00:05:38.700
about Foster's status post-Decimation by The
Huffington Post a few months later, they refused

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:43.949
to comment because it was a "potential spoiler,"
implying that the studio may still have plans

00:05:43.949 --> 00:05:45.480
for the character going forward.

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:51.260
Of course, Foster is one of the MCU’s leading
astrophysicists, so her skill set would certainly

00:05:51.260 --> 00:05:52.790
come in handy during Endgame.

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:57.820
But if nothing else, Jane and Thor could probably
both do with morale boost after the events

00:05:57.820 --> 00:06:01.360
of Infinity War — and a reunion could be
just the thing they need.

